IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `loa-dates`
IMPORT `loa-core`
IMPORT `loa-seat`

-- Limitation of Actions Act 1936 (SA) -- cases for the seat of the person bringing the action (loa-seat.l4). Every
-- expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (the section is named on each group), never copied from
-- the encoding's output; day counts are shown where they matter. Edges: 29 February, month ends, the 18th birthday and
-- the day before, the 30-year cap, the first and last days of the s 37(2) window and the day before it, the Act's own
-- Example in s 37(3), the commencement days 17 June 1993, 2 February 1994, 1 January 2006, 1 July 2021, the 12 months
-- of s 48(3)(b)(i) to the day, six years after the incident to the day (s 45A).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the person bringing the action`

`NOLIMIT` MEANS `no time limit: an action for damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child may be brought at any time and is not subject to any limitation period (s 3A(1)); the court may still dismiss or stay it if the lapse of time makes a fair trial impossible (s 3A(4))`

`NOREACH` MEANS `s 3A does not reach this: it covers abuse suffered while the person abused was a child, under 18 (s 3A(1), s 3(1)); the ordinary periods apply`

`NOTSAY3A` MEANS `the Act does not say: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 3A(5)), and the list is not closed`

`CL2` MEANS `yes: section 3A applies whenever the cause of action accrued, even if a limitation period had expired before 1 February 2019 (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 2)`

`CL3AB` MEANS `yes: you may commence an action even though an earlier action on the claim was started, whether or not it was finalised or was discontinued (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 3(1)(a), (b))`

`PERMITTED` MEANS `yes: the court has granted permission to commence the action despite the earlier judgment or dismissal on the limitation ground (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 3(2))`

`NEEDPERM` MEANS `not without permission: after a judgment or dismissal on the limitation ground, a new action may be commenced only if a court, satisfied that it is just and reasonable, grants permission (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 3(2))`

`NOHELP` MEANS `this transitional rule does not help: section 3A does not apply to the claim on these facts`

`P3A` MEANS `none: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 3A(1))`

`P36` MEANS `3 years after the cause of action accrued (s 36(1))`

`P36LATENT` MEANS `3 years after the injury first came to your knowledge, because it remained latent (s 36(1a))`

`P35` MEANS `6 years after the cause of action accrued (s 35)`

`P37EXT` MEANS `1 year running from the date of publication (s 37(1)), extended if a concerns notice is given in its last 56 days (s 37(2), (3))`

`P37` MEANS `1 year running from the date of publication (s 37(1))`

`P38` MEANS `6 years after the cause of action arose (s 38(1)(a))`

`P38TAX` MEANS `6 months after the date of the payment, and it cannot be extended (s 38(2)(a), (3))`

`P34` MEANS `15 years after the cause of action accrued or the judgment was recovered, or after the last written acknowledgment or part payment (s 34)`

`P33` MEANS `15 years after a present right to receive the money accrued, or after the last payment or written acknowledgment (s 33(1), (2))`

`PNCKIND` MEANS `not covered: a kind of action this encoding does not cover (Parts 2 and 3: land, rent, mortgages and trusts)`

`PNC38` MEANS `not covered: a restitution claim that arose before 17 June 1993 (s 38(1)(b): the old period or 6 years after 17 June 1993, whichever expired first)`

`PNCTAX` MEANS `not covered: a tax paid more than four months before 2 June 1994 (s 38(2)(b))`

`PNCDEF` MEANS `not covered: a publication before 1 January 2006, to which the limitation law before the Defamation Act 2005 applies`

`PNC36A` MEANS `not covered: a latent injury whose 3 years under s 36(1) had run out before s 36(1a) commenced on 8 February 2006`

`NOLASTDAY` MEANS `there is no last day: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 3A(1))`

`NOTSTARTED` MEANS `the time has not started: it runs from the return to the State of the person liable (s 39)`

`LNC` MEANS `not covered by this encoding`

`INTIME` MEANS `in time: it was done on or before the last day`

`LATEDONE` MEANS `late: it was done after the last day`

`STILL` MEANS `still in time: it has not been done yet and the last day has not passed`

`LATENOT` MEANS `late: it has not been done and the last day has passed`

`INTIME3A` MEANS `in time: there is no limitation period for an action for child abuse (s 3A)`

`STILL39` MEANS `still in time: the time has not started to run, because the person liable has not returned to the State (s 39)`

`TNC` MEANS `not covered: the time limit for this kind of action is not worked out here`

`NOTCHILD` MEANS `no: s 45A applies only where a child (under 18) suffers the personal injury (s 45A(1)(a))`

`NOTIPP` MEANS `no: s 45A applies only prospectively, and not to an injury from an incident before 1 May 2004 (Law Reform (Ipp Recommendations) Act 2004 Sch 1 cl 1)`

`NOTEXT` MEANS `no: the time for your action is not extended by this Act to more than 6 years after the incident, so s 45A(1) requires no notice`

`NOTORT` MEANS `no: notice need not be given to the person who actually committed an intentional tort when the action is brought against that person (s 45A(1) Exception)`

`NOTSAY45A` MEANS `the Act does not say whether s 45A applies to an action for child abuse, which has no limitation period (s 3A) rather than an extended one`

`COMPLIED` MEANS `nothing is lost: you complied with s 45A`

`EXCUSED` MEANS `nothing is lost: the court is satisfied that there is good reason to excuse the non-compliance (s 45A(7))`

`LOSE` MEANS `you may still sue, but no damages for medical or gratuitous services provided before the action was commenced, and no legal or other costs incurred in contemplation of the action, will be allowed (s 45A(7))`

`ABSENT` MEANS `no: being absent from the State gives you no further time (s 46)`

`PRISON` MEANS `no: being imprisoned gives you no further time (s 46)`

`S47NOHELP` MEANS `s 47 does not help: the other law already allows at least twelve months from when the cause of action arose`

`S47CRIM` MEANS `no: s 47 does not apply to a criminal action (s 47(2)(a))`

`S47ELEC` MEANS `no: s 47 does not apply to an action to try the validity of an election or of title to an office (s 47(2)(b))`

`S47LG` MEANS `no: s 47 does not apply to an action to try the validity of a local government assessment, rate or loan (s 47(2)(c))`

`S47ESS` MEANS `no: the court is of the opinion that the limitation is essential to the nature or purpose of the action (s 47(2)(d))`

`S48CRIM` MEANS `no: s 48 does not apply to criminal proceedings (s 48(3)(a))`

`S48TAX` MEANS `no: the period for recovering an invalid tax cannot be extended (s 38(3))`

`S48OTHER` MEANS `possibly: the court may extend a time limit set by another law to the extent, and on the terms, the justice of the case requires (s 48(1)); the claim must be endorsed with a statement that you seek an extension under s 48 (s 48(4))`

`S48NOGROUND` MEANS `no: neither ground in s 48(3)(b) is met (a material fact learnt in the last 12 months of the period or after it, with the action instituted within 12 months of learning it; or a reasonable delay caused by the defendant's representations or conduct)`

`S48NOTJUST` MEANS `no: a ground in s 48(3)(b) is met, but the court is not satisfied that in all the circumstances it is just to extend (s 48(3), (3b))`

`S48YES` MEANS `yes: the court may extend the time (s 48(1), (3)); the claim must be endorsed with a statement that you seek an extension under s 48 (s 48(4))`

`S50NA` MEANS `s 50 does not arise: no law requires you to give notice before the action`

`S50YES` MEANS `yes: the court may dispense with the requirement to give notice before the action, at any time before or after the close of pleadings (s 50)`

`S50NO` MEANS `no: the court dispenses with a notice requirement only if the justice of the case requires it (s 50)`

`NC37A` MEANS `not covered: s 37A applies to later publications on or after 1 July 2021 (2020 Act Sch 1 cl 5(2), (3))`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
`LAST` d MEANS `the last day to commence the action is` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
`ATLATEST` d MEANS `the time is extended while the incapacity continues, but not beyond 30 years after the right arose (s 45(1), (3)); at the latest` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
`NOTICEINS` d MEANS `yes: give notice of the intended action to the relevant third-party insurer (s 45A(1), (2)), within 6 years after the incident, by` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
`NOTICEOTHER` d MEANS `yes: give notice of the intended action to each other person alleged to be liable, not the person who committed the intentional tort (s 45A(1) Exception), by` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
`NOTICEALL` d MEANS `yes: give notice of the intended action to each person alleged to be liable in damages (s 45A(1)), by` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
`TWELVE` d MEANS `you may bring it at any time within twelve months from when the cause of action arose, by` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
`FROMFIRST` d MEANS `your time for the later publication runs from the first publication (s 37A(2)), on` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
`FROMLATER` d MEANS `your time for the later publication runs from that later publication itself, on` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
`EXT37B` d MEANS `the court may extend the period, if you satisfy it that it is just and reasonable to allow the action to proceed, up to 3 years from the publication (s 37B(2)), that is to` d

`NO37B` MEANS `no: the court may extend the period only if the plaintiff satisfies it that it is just and reasonable to allow the action to proceed (s 37B(2))`

`NC37B` MEANS `not covered: s 37B applies to publications on or after 1 July 2021 (2020 Act Sch 1 cl 5(4))`

§§ `Shorthands for the facts`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
D d m y MEANS `the date` d m y

`any day` MEANS D 1 1 2000
`an adult's birth date` MEANS D 1 1 1970

`ABUSE` MEANS `damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child`
`PI` MEANS `damages that include damages for personal injuries`
`S35` MEANS `simple contract, tort, account, or another action listed in s 35, with no damages for personal injuries`
`DEF` MEANS `defamation`
`RESTITUTION` MEANS `recovery of money paid by mistake or on other restitutionary grounds`
`TAX` MEANS `recovery of money paid as a tax that was invalid`
`SPECIALTY` MEANS `rent under a lease by deed, or covenant or debt on a bond, other specialty, judgment or recognisance`
`CHARGE` MEANS `money secured by a mortgage, judgment or lien or otherwise charged on land, or a legacy`
`OTHER` MEANS `another kind of action`

-- An adult's action with none of the extensions.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`, a IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`plain last day` k a MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k a FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` `an adult's birth date` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day`

GIVEN b IS A DATE, k IS A `Kind of action`, a IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`last day for a person born` b `for` k a MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k a FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` b FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day`

GIVEN b IS A DATE, a IS A DATE, s IS A DATE, fin IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`personal injury last day born` b `accrued` a `incapable from` s `ended` fin `on` e MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` `PI` a FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` b TRUE s fin e FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`, a IS A DATE, back IS A BOOLEAN, r IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`last day when they were absent` k a `returned` back `on` r MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k a FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE back r `an adult's birth date` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day`

GIVEN a IS A DATE, death IS A DATE, grant IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`estate last day` a `died` death `granted` grant MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` `PI` a FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` `an adult's birth date` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE death grant FALSE `any day`

GIVEN p IS A DATE, n IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`defamation last day` p `notice on` n MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` `DEF` p FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` `an adult's birth date` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` TRUE n

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`, a IS A DATE, done IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A DATE, t IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`in time?` k a done c t MEANS
    `Was my action commenced in time` k a FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` `an adult's birth date` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day` done c t

§§ `s 3A: no limitation period for child abuse`

#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `sexual abuse` 10 EQUALS `NOLIMIT`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `serious physical abuse` 17 EQUALS `NOLIMIT`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse` 5 EQUALS `NOLIMIT`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `sexual abuse` 18 EQUALS `NOREACH`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `physical abuse that was not serious` 12 EQUALS `NOTSAY3A`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `psychological abuse not related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse` 5 EQUALS `NOTSAY3A`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `another kind of abuse` 9 EQUALS `NOTSAY3A`

§§ `2018 Act Sch 1 cll 2, 3: claims barred before 1 February 2019`

#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred before` `sexual abuse` 10 `there was no earlier action or judgment` FALSE EQUALS `CL2`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred before` `sexual abuse` 10 `an action was started but not finalised before 1 February 2019` FALSE EQUALS `CL3AB`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred before` `serious physical abuse` 14 `an action was started but discontinued before 1 February 2019` FALSE EQUALS `CL3AB`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred before` `sexual abuse` 10 `a judgment was given on the ground that the limitation period had expired` FALSE EQUALS `NEEDPERM`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred before` `sexual abuse` 10 `an action was dismissed on the ground that the limitation period had expired` TRUE EQUALS `PERMITTED`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred before` `sexual abuse` 20 `a judgment was given on the ground that the limitation period had expired` TRUE EQUALS `NOHELP`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred before` `another kind of abuse` 10 `there was no earlier action or judgment` FALSE EQUALS `NOHELP`

§§ `ss 3A, 33-38: which period`

#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `ABUSE` (D 1 1 1990) FALSE EQUALS `P3A`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `PI` (D 15 3 2020) FALSE EQUALS `P36`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `PI` (D 15 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS `P36LATENT`
-- s 36(1a) commenced 8 February 2006: a latent injury accrued 7 February 2003 had its s 36(1) 3 years end on
-- 7 February 2006, before it (not covered); one accrued a day later was still running then (fork F14).
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `PI` (D 7 2 2003) TRUE EQUALS `PNC36A`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `PI` (D 8 2 2003) TRUE EQUALS `P36LATENT`
#ASSERT `By when must I commence my action` `PI` (D 7 2 2003) TRUE (D 1 1 2010) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` `an adult's birth date` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `LNC`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `S35` (D 15 3 2020) FALSE EQUALS `P35`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `DEF` (D 31 12 2005) FALSE EQUALS `PNCDEF`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `DEF` (D 1 1 2006) FALSE EQUALS `P37`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `DEF` (D 30 6 2021) FALSE EQUALS `P37`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `DEF` (D 1 7 2021) FALSE EQUALS `P37EXT`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `RESTITUTION` (D 16 6 1993) FALSE EQUALS `PNC38`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `RESTITUTION` (D 17 6 1993) FALSE EQUALS `P38`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `TAX` (D 1 2 1994) FALSE EQUALS `PNCTAX`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `TAX` (D 2 2 1994) FALSE EQUALS `P38TAX`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `SPECIALTY` (D 1 7 2000) FALSE EQUALS `P34`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `CHARGE` (D 5 5 2005) FALSE EQUALS `P33`
#ASSERT `Which limitation period applies to my action` `OTHER` (D 5 5 2005) FALSE EQUALS `PNCKIND`

§§ `ss 33-38: the last day, with no extension (fork F1: the same day of the month)`

#ASSERT `plain last day` `PI` (D 15 3 2020) EQUALS `LAST` (D 15 3 2023)
#ASSERT `plain last day` `PI` (D 29 2 2020) EQUALS `LAST` (D 28 2 2023)
#ASSERT `plain last day` `S35` (D 31 8 2019) EQUALS `LAST` (D 31 8 2025)
#ASSERT `plain last day` `RESTITUTION` (D 10 10 2019) EQUALS `LAST` (D 10 10 2025)
#ASSERT `plain last day` `TAX` (D 31 8 2023) EQUALS `LAST` (D 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `plain last day` `SPECIALTY` (D 1 7 2000) EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 7 2015)
#ASSERT `plain last day` `CHARGE` (D 5 5 2005) EQUALS `LAST` (D 5 5 2020)
#ASSERT `plain last day` `DEF` (D 10 8 2022) EQUALS `LAST` (D 10 8 2023)
#ASSERT `plain last day` `ABUSE` (D 1 1 1990) EQUALS `NOLASTDAY`
#ASSERT `plain last day` `OTHER` (D 1 1 2020) EQUALS `LNC`
#ASSERT `plain last day` `RESTITUTION` (D 16 6 1993) EQUALS `LNC`

§§ `s 36(1a): a latent injury (accrued 1 June 2010, known 10 September 2024)`

#ASSERT `By when must I commence my action` `PI` (D 1 6 2010) TRUE (D 10 9 2024) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` `an adult's birth date` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `LAST` (D 10 9 2027)

§§ `s 45(3) and s 36(1a): the 30-year cap stops an extension; it does not shorten a latent injury's period`

-- Accrued 1 January 2005, known 1 January 2033: the s 36(1a) period ends 1 January 2036, past the 30-year day
-- (1 January 2035). An adult has 1 January 2036; a person born 1 January 2000 (a child when it accrued) has the same,
-- not less: s 45 cannot extend past 1 January 2035, but the unextended period stands.
#ASSERT `By when must I commence my action` `PI` (D 1 1 2005) TRUE (D 1 1 2033) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` `an adult's birth date` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 1 2036)
#ASSERT `By when must I commence my action` `PI` (D 1 1 2005) TRUE (D 1 1 2033) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` (D 1 1 2000) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 1 2036)
-- Known 1 January 2036 and the incapacity (from 1 January 2030) still continuing: the period ends 1 January 2039,
-- after the 30-year day, so that is the last day (not "at the latest 1 January 2035").
#ASSERT `By when must I commence my action` `PI` (D 1 1 2005) TRUE (D 1 1 2036) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` (D 1 1 2000) TRUE (D 1 1 2030) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 1 2039)
-- Known 1 January 2030 (period ends 1 January 2033, before the 30-year day): childhood (4749 days) extends it, capped
-- at 1 January 2035.
#ASSERT `By when must I commence my action` `PI` (D 1 1 2005) TRUE (D 1 1 2030) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` (D 1 1 2000) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 1 2035)

§§ `ss 33(2), 34: a later acknowledgment or part payment`

#ASSERT `By when must I commence my action` `SPECIALTY` (D 1 7 2000) FALSE `any day` TRUE (D 3 4 2010) FALSE FALSE `any day` `an adult's birth date` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `LAST` (D 3 4 2025)
#ASSERT `By when must I commence my action` `CHARGE` (D 5 5 2005) FALSE `any day` TRUE (D 6 6 2016) FALSE FALSE `any day` `an adult's birth date` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `LAST` (D 6 6 2031)

§§ `s 39: the person liable absent from the State when it accrued`

#ASSERT `last day when they were absent` `S35` (D 1 3 2020) `returned` TRUE `on` (D 15 7 2021) EQUALS `LAST` (D 15 7 2027)
#ASSERT `last day when they were absent` `PI` (D 1 3 2020) `returned` TRUE `on` (D 15 7 2021) EQUALS `LAST` (D 15 7 2024)
#ASSERT `last day when they were absent` `S35` (D 1 3 2020) `returned` FALSE `on` `any day` EQUALS `NOTSTARTED`
-- s 39 reaches only ss 35 and 36 actions: defamation runs from publication regardless.
#ASSERT `last day when they were absent` `DEF` (D 1 3 2022) `returned` FALSE `on` `any day` EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 3 2023)

§§ `s 45: childhood (worked by days; the answer falls on the 18th birthday plus the period)`

-- Born 10 May 2008, injured 1 March 2015: 4088 days of childhood; 1 March 2018 plus 4088 days is 10 May 2029.
#ASSERT `last day for a person born` (D 10 5 2008) `for` `PI` (D 1 3 2015) EQUALS `LAST` (D 10 5 2029)
-- Born 1 January 2010, injured the next day: 6573 days; 2 January 2013 plus 6573 days is 1 January 2031.
#ASSERT `last day for a person born` (D 1 1 2010) `for` `PI` (D 2 1 2010) EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 1 2031)
-- s 45(3): born 1 June 2000, judgment 1 June 2001; 15 years plus 6209 days would be 1 June 2033, capped at 1 June 2031.
#ASSERT `last day for a person born` (D 1 6 2000) `for` `SPECIALTY` (D 1 6 2001) EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 6 2031)
-- s 33(3): for a legacy, s 45 counts from the last acknowledgment (1 January 2010, aged 10): 2922 days of childhood
-- after it; 1 January 2025 plus 2922 days is 1 January 2033 (counting from 1 January 2005 would give 1 January 2038).
#ASSERT `By when must I commence my action` `CHARGE` (D 1 1 2005) FALSE `any day` TRUE (D 1 1 2010) FALSE FALSE `any day` (D 1 1 2000) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 1 2033)
-- Injured on the 18th birthday: no longer a child, no extension.
#ASSERT `last day for a person born` (D 1 3 2002) `for` `PI` (D 1 3 2020) EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 3 2023)
-- The day before: one day of childhood.
#ASSERT `last day for a person born` (D 2 3 2002) `for` `PI` (D 1 3 2020) EQUALS `LAST` (D 2 3 2023)
-- s 38(3): the invalid tax period cannot be extended, even for a child.
#ASSERT `last day for a person born` (D 1 1 2010) `for` `TAX` (D 31 8 2023) EQUALS `LAST` (D 29 2 2024)

§§ `s 45: mental incapacity`

-- Incapable 1 April to 1 October 2020 (183 days) from accrual on 1 April 2020: 1 April 2023 plus 183 days.
#ASSERT `personal injury last day born` `an adult's birth date` `accrued` (D 1 4 2020) `incapable from` (D 1 4 2020) `ended` TRUE `on` (D 1 10 2020) EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 10 2023)
-- Incapable later, 1 January to 1 February 2021 (31 days): 1 April 2023 plus 31 days.
#ASSERT `personal injury last day born` `an adult's birth date` `accrued` (D 1 4 2020) `incapable from` (D 1 1 2021) `ended` TRUE `on` (D 1 2 2021) EQUALS `LAST` (D 2 5 2023)
-- Incapable from before accrual: only the days after the right arose count.
#ASSERT `personal injury last day born` `an adult's birth date` `accrued` (D 1 4 2020) `incapable from` (D 1 1 2019) `ended` TRUE `on` (D 1 10 2020) EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 10 2023)
-- Still incapable: extended while it continues, to 30 years at the latest.
#ASSERT `personal injury last day born` `an adult's birth date` `accrued` (D 1 4 2020) `incapable from` (D 1 4 2020) `ended` FALSE `on` `any day` EQUALS `ATLATEST` (D 1 4 2050)
-- Childhood and incapacity overlapping (born 1 January 2005, injured 1 January 2020, incapable 1 June 2022 to 1 June
-- 2023): 1096 + 365 - 214 = 1247 days; 1 January 2023 plus 1247 days is 1 June 2026.
#ASSERT `personal injury last day born` (D 1 1 2005) `accrued` (D 1 1 2020) `incapable from` (D 1 6 2022) `ended` TRUE `on` (D 1 6 2023) EQUALS `LAST` (D 1 6 2026)

§§ `s 46A: an action that survives for an estate`

-- Death 1 March 2022, grant 1 September 2022 (184 days, less than twelve months): 10 January 2025 plus 184 days.
#ASSERT `estate last day` (D 10 1 2022) `died` (D 1 3 2022) `granted` (D 1 9 2022) EQUALS `LAST` (D 13 7 2025)
-- Grant two years after the death: the twelve months is the lesser.
#ASSERT `estate last day` (D 10 1 2022) `died` (D 1 3 2022) `granted` (D 1 3 2024) EQUALS `LAST` (D 10 1 2026)

§§ `s 37(2), (3): a concerns notice in the last 56 days (published 10 August 2022; last day 10 August 2023)`

-- The Example: notice 7 days before expiry, 6 days left, extended by 50 days.
#ASSERT `defamation last day` (D 10 8 2022) `notice on` (D 4 8 2023) EQUALS `LAST` (D 29 9 2023)
-- The first day of the window (55 days left: extended by 1).
#ASSERT `defamation last day` (D 10 8 2022) `notice on` (D 16 6 2023) EQUALS `LAST` (D 11 8 2023)
-- One day before the window: no extension.
#ASSERT `defamation last day` (D 10 8 2022) `notice on` (D 15 6 2023) EQUALS `LAST` (D 10 8 2023)
-- On the last day itself (no days left: extended by 56).
#ASSERT `defamation last day` (D 10 8 2022) `notice on` (D 10 8 2023) EQUALS `LAST` (D 5 10 2023)
-- A publication before 1 July 2021: s 37(2) as amended does not apply (2020 Act Sch 1 cl 5(1)).
#ASSERT `defamation last day` (D 30 6 2021) `notice on` (D 25 6 2022) EQUALS `LAST` (D 30 6 2022)

